From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Flavius <Flavius256@icloud.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 21:47:04 +0000
Subject: register arguments

Pass the arguments the console left in registers.

The C relied on a register still holding a value at a call (a0-a3, $f12-$f15) or on a
function's result left in $v0/$f0. On the console that works; translated by hostgen for the
port, the callee gets 0 or a stale value. Each function now takes and passes what the retail
code passes. Same registers, no move added, so the PS2 build is unchanged.

- get_help_message_text (FUN_001fdd10): the message id is a parameter, passed on to the index
  search. The C took no argument and relied on the id still in a0; translated, every message was
  message 0's (the title menu showed a weapon tip). Commit 0a6feb65.
- setup_level_cameras (FUN_L00_001ed358): clear_vector and normalize_vector_xyz declared with
  __asm__("func_001F99F8") and __asm__("FUN_001f9bf8"). The plain names are no symbol of this
  build; the retail code calls those two (jal at 0x1ED408 and 0x1ED428).
- FUN_L00_001ed630: takes (a, b, c) and passes b, c to subtract_vector_xyz. The C took one
  argument and called the subtraction with one; the retail code leaves the caller's a1 and a2 in
  place for it, and every caller passes them.
- FUN_L00_002e48a0: takes the scale as a second (float) parameter and passes it to the first
  FUN_001f9a68. The C dropped it; the retail code passes the caller's $f12 on. Translated, the
  scale came out as 0.
- refresh_point_light (FUN_00201f58): detach_point_light and create_point_light declared with
  their s32 parameter, and the light index passed to the first. The C called
  detach_point_light() with nothing and relied on a0 still holding the index (the retail code
  moves it to s0 only for the second call, in the first jal's delay slot). The call goes through
  each level's own copy (a folded wrapper), so translated it went through a K&R pointer with no
  argument: on Aridia (level 2) the light code read a host address as a game one and the program
  stopped.
- transform_scaled_vertex_batch (FUN_0020cd48): func_002106F8 declared with its four parameters,
  and object, count, point_indices, cursor passed. The C called it with (void) and relied on
  a0-a3 still holding the caller's arguments (the jal at 0x20CD7C, its delay slot a float
  multiply); translated, the callee got four zeros and built no point table. Checked against
  config/us/expected/asm/rendering/geometry/transform_scaled_vertex_batch/FUN_0020cd48.s, not
  rebuilt.
- FUN_L00_00262cf0: takes (a, b, scale, yaw, pitch) and passes the three floats to
  build_spherical_offset. The C took two arguments and called the offset builder with only the
  buffer; the retail code leaves the caller's $f12-$f14 in place for it (jal at 0x27B530 with no
  float setup), and every caller passes them. Translated, the offset came out from zero scale
  and angles.
- FUN_L00_0023e838: detach_point_light declared with its int parameter, and i passed. The C
  called detach_point_light() with nothing and relied on a0 still holding i (the retail jal
  FUN_00201f88 has daddu $16, $4, $0 in its delay slot and a0 untouched); translated, the light
  index was 0.
- force_help_message (FUN_002151d8): try_set_help_message declared with (s32, s32) and passed
  owner, message_id. The C called it with nothing and relied on a0/a1 still holding them (jal
  FUN_00215130 with the arguments untouched); translated, the owner and message were 0. Checked
  against the assembly, not rebuilt.
- get_occlusion_grid_from_pair (FUN_001f2768): returns s32, the result of the last
  parse_occlusion_grid; the first call passes the first cell's x, y, z. The C returned void and
  called the first lookup with no arguments (a0-a2 left in place, delay slot nop);
  build_occlusion_visibility reads the result as the grid pointer. Checked against the assembly,
  not rebuilt.
- FUN_L14_002b5730: FUN_L00_0025d808 declared with its six parameters and passed the caller's
  f12. The retail code leaves $f12 in place for the call; the C passed five arguments and the
  float was 0. Same registers, no move added.
- is_value_within_interpolated_window (FUN_00214cc8): compute_interpolated_record_value declared
  with its pointer parameter, and anim passed. The C called it with nothing and relied on a0
  still holding anim (the retail jal FUN_0020c9e0 follows daddu $16, $4, $0, a0 untouched);
  translated, the keyframe record was read from a stale register.
- clamp_voice_position_to_collision (FUN_0022c5a8): random_spherical_offset declared with its
  s32 first parameter, and position passed. The C called it with the two floats only and relied
  on a0 still holding position (the retail jal FUN_00213358 has daddu $16, $4, $0 in its delay
  slot, a0 untouched); translated, the offset was written to a stale pointer. Checked against
  build/baseline/config/us/expected/asm/audio/sound/fun_0022c5a8/FUN_0022c5a8.s, not rebuilt.
- FUN_L00_0020d540: takes slot and passes it to FUN_L00_0020d498. The C took no argument and
  called the slot lookup with nothing; the retail jal FUN_L00_0020d498
  (config/us/overlays/asm/FUN_L00_0020d540.s) leaves the caller's a0 in place, and the one
  caller passes the slot index. Same registers, no move added. Not rebuilt.
- resolve_camera_surface_height (FUN_002135f0): sample_surface_height_map declared with its
  second (s32) parameter and optional_output passed to it. The C dropped it; the retail code
  leaves the caller's a1 in place (it is saved to s1 first, and jal follows with a1 untouched),
  so the callee fills the normal there. Translated, the normal pointer was 0 and the normal
  never written.
- FUN_L00_002336e8: takes (out, in, x) and passes out, in, -x to FUN_L00_002334d0. The C took
  one argument and called with one; the retail code negates $f12 and jumps with a0 and a1
  untouched (neg.s in the delay slot of the jal). Translated, both vector pointers were 0.
- FUN_L00_0025da70: returns the float of FUN_001f9b80 or FUN_001f9b48 (declared float). The C
  returned void; the retail code leaves that result in $f0, and FUN_L00_0025dcd8 and
  FUN_L00_0025df68 read it as the distance.
- FUN_L00_0024f3e0: FUN_L00_0024f190 called as advance_moby_animation_blend (its definition in
  the same file, with its two parameters) and a0, a1 passed. The C called it with nothing; the
  retail code passes its own a0 and a1 (the second is the animation state the callee works on).
  Translated, the state pointer was 0.
- FUN_L00_00263ac8 (level 0's copy, the one attach_manipulator is called from):
  attach_manipulator declared with its three parameters, and (void *)owner_moby, slot_index,
  manipulator passed. The C called it with nothing and relied on a0-a2 still holding the
  caller's arguments (jal FUN_0020cb10 at 0x263AFC, delay slot nop, daddu $16, $6, $0 at entry
  and no move before the call); translated, the manipulator was attached to a stale owner. Same
  registers, no move added. Checked against
  build/overlay-asm/level_00/split/f00263AC8/FUN_L00_00263ac8.s, not rebuilt.
- extract_matrix_rotation_quaternion (FUN_002144d8): copy_matrix_rotation declared with its
  second (s32) parameter and passed destination_matrix. The C called it with the buffer alone;
  the retail code leaves the caller's a1 in $5 for it, and FUN_001fa298 reads its source from
  there (a copy of the destination matrix into the scratch buffer). Translated, the source was
  0.
- FUN_L01_002b8288 (water ripple wrapper): takes (a, b, x, y, radius, amount) and passes the
  four floats on to FUN_L00_002a3ec8 after the 0 mode. The C took two arguments and called the
  ripple with three; the retail code is jal FUN_L00_002a3ec8 with only daddu $6, $0, $0 in the
  delay slot, leaving the caller's $f12-$f15 in place (its callers in rocket.c and
  taxi_platform.c pass them). Translated, every ripple had zero position, radius and strength.
  Checked against the assembly, not rebuilt.
- FUN_L00_0020f160 (hero hand-matrix smoothing): takes (arg, entry) and passes entry to
  copy_matrix3x4_alt (FUN_001fa2b8) as its source. The C took one argument and called the
  48-byte copy with only its destination; the retail code leaves the caller's a1 (its only
  caller, FUN_L00_0020f580, passes D_0013FE10 + index * 0x40 there) in place for the jal at
  0x20F1B4 and never touches it before. Translated, the copy read its source from a 0. Checked
  against build/overlay-asm/level_00/split/f0020F160/FUN_L00_0020f160.s, not rebuilt.
- FUN_L00_0020fca8 (removes Ratchet's hand items): the item's update pointer takes the moby and
  is called as item_moby->fn(item_moby). The C called it with no argument; the retail code loads
  the moby into $4 before the jalr, so the update gets it. Translated, the update (the wrench's,
  FUN_L00_002a84c8) got a garbage moby and the pause menu's Weapons page crashed once the menu's
  hooks reached this function (957f9ffb).
- FUN_L00_00236458 (the air meter's update, its stars): takes the HUD element e and passes it to
  FUN_L00_00235ea0. The C took no argument and called the counter update with nothing; the
  retail code (config/us/overlays/asm/FUN_L00_00236458.s) does jal FUN_L00_00235ea0 first thing
  with a0 untouched (delay slot nop), and the HUD loop (FUN_L00_0023ac78) calls the element's
  update with the element in a0. Translated, the element was 0 and its value pointer was read
  from game address 0xC: on Pokitaru (level 11) the game stopped at 0x05550555 as soon as
  Ratchet dived. Same registers, no move added. Not rebuilt.
- FUN_L07_00281ef8: takes (id, idx, a, b) and passes idx, a, b to FUN_L00_002591d0. The C took
  one argument and called the group lookup with only &current; the retail jal FUN_L00_002591d0
  at 0x281F08 (delay slot daddu $4, $29, $0) leaves the caller's a1-a3 in place, and the taxi
  platform passes (m, group, 1, 0). Translated, every lookup was of group 0 with both flags
  clear (46,848 calls on Umbris in a regression run). PAL's matched func_L07_00282EB0 already
  does this. Not rebuilt.
- FUN_L02_002a40d0: takes the scale as a second (float) parameter and passes it on to
  FUN_L02_002a4058. The retail code only sets a1 to 0x80 in the delay slot of the jal at
  0x2A40D8 and leaves the caller's $f12 in place (electric_gate.c passes 1.0); translated, the
  table was scaled by 0. PAL's func_L02_002A52B0 already does this. Not rebuilt.
- FUN_L04_002927d0: takes (moby, rig, t) and passes t to walker_gait_mask (FUN_L00_002a13f0,
  declared (int *, float)). The C passed rig where the mask takes its float; retail leaves the
  caller's $f12 in place for the jal at 0x29280C (both callers declare the float) and the mask
  never reads a1. PAL's LegRig_GetAnimMode already does this. Not rebuilt.
- FUN_L09_0021e560, FUN_L09_0021e8c0: the strip builder takes (tex0, tex1, fraction) and passes
  fraction to FUN_L02_0024fca0 (declared with its seventh, float parameter); FUN_L09_0021e8c0's
  unused float is that fraction, passed on. Neither function touches $f12 before its jal
  (0x21E690, 0x21E90C), so the caller's float reaches the interpolation; translated, it was 0.
  Not rebuilt.
- video_dec_end_put (FUN_0023cc10): takes (video_dec, bytes) and passes bytes to vi_buf_end_put
  (declared (s32, s32)). Retail only adds 0x48 to a0 in the delay slot of the jal at 0x23CC18
  and leaves a1 in place; both callers pass the count. Translated, the buffer was advanced by 0
  bytes. Not rebuilt.
- FUN_L00_002ea7a0: takes the camera as its parameter and passes it to FUN_L00_002e9ef0. The C
  took nothing and called the reset with nothing; retail leaves the caller's a0 in place for the
  jal at 0x2EA7E4, and FUN_L00_002e9ef0 reads p + 0x70. Not rebuilt.
- the grab-check wrappers FUN_L00_002cadc0, FUN_L00_002d56e0, FUN_L01_002efa88,
  FUN_L01_002f1c78, FUN_L02_002d61c0, FUN_L06_002ea5e0, FUN_L11_00316160, FUN_L12_002e16b8,
  FUN_L17_002efea8, FUN_L18_002d6108, FUN_L18_002fcbb0: each takes (moby, pos, target) and
  passes pos, target to FUN_L00_002db8f8 (a _pt declaration with its three parameters). Each
  wrapper only moves a0 to s0 in the jal's delay slot and leaves the caller's a1, a2 in place
  (every level copy checked), and FUN_L00_002db8f8 reads both. PAL's matched copies
  (func_L00_002CC210 and the others) already pass them. Not rebuilt.
- FUN_L01_002efaf8, FUN_L02_002d6210, FUN_L06_002ea6a8, FUN_L11_00316210, FUN_L12_002e1758,
  FUN_L18_002d6190: each takes (moby, quad) and passes quad to FUN_L00_002dbb20. As above, for
  the second argument (a1), which FUN_L00_002dbb20 reads. Not rebuilt.
- FUN_L00_002da218 (a carried moby's class hook 4, the placing): takes (moby, b) and passes b to
  the hook. The C took one argument; the retail code
  (build/overlay-asm/level_00/split/f002DA218/FUN_L00_002da1e0.s) never touches a1 before its
  jalr, and its one caller (FUN_L00_002dc9f0, a moby flying into the Suck Cannon) passes the
  cannon's muzzle there, where the hook (FUN_L00_002dbb20) puts the moby. Translated, the hook
  got a stale register for its position. Same registers, no move added. Not rebuilt (PAL's
  func_L00_002DB6C8 with the same change builds EXACT).
- FUN_L00_002cadc0, FUN_L00_002d56e0, FUN_L01_002efaf8, FUN_L01_002f1c78, FUN_L02_002d61c0,
  FUN_L06_002ea6a8, FUN_L11_00316210, FUN_L12_002e1758, FUN_L17_002efea8, FUN_L18_002d6190,
  FUN_L18_002fcbb0 (the Suck Cannon hooks of its targets' classes): each takes (moby, position,
  target, float height) and passes all four to its callee, declared so (FUN_L00_002db8f8_h,
  FUN_L00_002dbb20_h). The catalogue folds each class's grab, place and fire wrappers into one
  name, and each copy calls its own of FUN_L00_002db8f8, FUN_L00_002dbb20 and the fire
  FUN_L00_002dbc30 (moby, velocity, target, height); the retail code touches none of a1, a2 and
  $f12 before its jal (e.g. build/overlay-asm/level_06/split/f002EA6A8/FUN_L06_002ea6a8.s). The
  port runs each copy's own callee (hostgen, openrac_call_in_copy), so the fire got a stale
  target and height from the C that took two or three. Same registers, no move added. Not
  rebuilt (PAL's same change to its eleven builds EXACT).
- hud_update_counter (FUN_L00_00235ea0): its __asm__ label on a declaration of its own before
  the old-style definition, not after the parameter declaration. void f(e) HudElem *e
  __asm__(".."); labels the parameter, which Clang refuses, so hostgen left the whole file out.
  Same symbol, same instructions; not rebuilt.
